version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23080487"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kaganyurtk/sparse-trajectory-reconstruction"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23080487"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility materials for unconstrained and kinematically constrained
  neural-network studies of rocket-trajectory reconstruction. The archive
  includes RQ1 training and evaluation code and recovered experiment packages
  with NEXT-5, Iridium-family and RQ2 reconstruction v1.1 runners, manifests,
  splits, checkpoints and historical verification records. RQ2 uses sparse
  reconstruction inputs with complete fitting targets and dataset-specific
  weights. Third-party raw telemetry is excluded. Execution requires permitted
  source data and historical-path configuration; clean-environment end-to-end
  replay is not claimed. Code is MIT; author-written documentation is CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - rocket telemetry
  - trajectory reconstruction
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - kinematic constraints
  - sparse observations
  - reproducibility
